-- title:
--   Theta section cutting out the locus h⁰(M(dε))≠ 0
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and $c\colon C\to\operatorname{Spec} k$ a proper morphism which is smooth of relative dimension $1$, and let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$, i.e. a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} k\to C$ whose composite with $c$ is the identity. Assume the degrees occurring in finite-map chart data for $(c,\varepsilon)$ are unbounded: for every $m_0$ there is a `SmoothProperCurve.FiniteMapData c ε` with $m\ge m_0$, that is, affine opens $U,V$ with $U\sqcup V$-union all of $C$, $U$ the complement of the image of $\varepsilon$, sections $f\in\Gamma(C,U)$, $g\in\Gamma(C,V)$ cutting out $U\cap V$ as a basic open set and restricting to mutually inverse units there, with $\Gamma(C,U)$, $\Gamma(C,V)$ finite over the polynomial algebras generated by $f$, resp. $g$, and with all $f$-level sets over local $k$-algebras finite free of rank $m$. Let $t\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec} k$ be locally of finite type and let $M$ be a rigidified line bundle for $(c,\varepsilon,t)$: an invertible module $M.L$ on $C\times_k T$ together with a trivialisation of its pullback along the induced section. Fix $r,n,d\in\mathbb N$ with $d+n=r$, and write $\mathcal O(m\varepsilon)$ for `sectionTwist c ε t m`, the dual of the module of the $m$-th power of the ideal sheaf of the section. Assume that for every field $K$, every $s\colon\operatorname{Spec} K\to T$ and every cover $\mathcal W$ of the fibre $C_s=(C\times_k T)\times_T\operatorname{Spec} K$ by two affine opens with affine intersection, the two-chart Čech complex of the restriction of $M.L\otimes\mathcal O(r\varepsilon)$ to $C_s$ has subsingleton $H^1$ and $\dim_K H^0=n$. Then there is a global section $\theta$ of `thetaBundle c ε t M r n`, the dual of the $n$-th determinant of `picardBundle c ε t M (sectionTwist c ε t r)`, such that for every field $K$ and every $s\colon\operatorname{Spec} K\to T$, the pullback of $\theta$ along $s$ vanishes if and only if for every such two-affine cover $\mathcal W$ of $C_s$ the Čech $H^0$ of the restriction of $M.L\otimes\mathcal O(d\varepsilon)$ is nontrivial.
--
--   This is the determinant-of-evaluation construction of the theta divisor in the relative setting: the pushforward of $M(r\varepsilon)$ is locally free of rank $n$ by cohomology and base change, the $n$-th thickening of the section contributes a second sheaf of the same rank, and the determinant of the evaluation map between them is a section of the dual determinant of the Picard bundle whose zero locus on field-valued points is exactly the locus where $h^0(M(d\varepsilon))\neq 0$. It is used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.exists_pullbackSection_thetaBundle_poincare_eq_zero_iff`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.exists_pullbackSection_thetaBundle_poincare_eq_zero_iff), which specialises the construction to the Poincaré bundle.
